    "result_text": "All requirements are satisfied and the build is green. The only remaining mentions of the old field names are in the acceptance test asserting they've been removed.\n\n## Summary\n\nI unified `customerCode` and `membershipNumber` into a single `memberId` field formatted `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>`, and removed the standalone `checkDigit`. The test suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1/1 tests green).\n\n**What changed:**\n\n- **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 renamed the persisted `customer_code`/`customerCode` field to `member_id`/`memberId` (getter/setter renamed); `primaryIdentifier()` now returns the memberId.\n\n- **`service/ClinicServiceImpl.java`** \u2014 replaced `generateCustomerCode` with `generateMemberId`, which assembles `REGION + FY + HASH8 + CHK`:\n  - `REGION` from the existing postcode/city region derivation,\n  - `FY` = 2-digit fiscal year of the business-day-adjusted registration date,\n  - `HASH8` = the same SHA-256-over-(telephone+lastName) first-8-upper-hex used by the region-and-hash identity,\n  - `CHK` = a single Luhn check digit over the digits of `REGION+FY+HASH8` (added a private `luhnCheckDigit` helper).\n  - Collision handling now applies to the **memberId** (appends `-<n>` from 2 upward against existing member ids).\n\n- **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 removed the `membershipNumber` and `checkDigit` mappings/methods; `formatLocality` now takes the region as the leading letter-run of the memberId (before the FY digits), so `locality` \u2192 `timezone` \u2192 `ownerSegment` all reference the memberId. `memberId` itself is auto-mapped by name.\n\n- **`audit/OwnerAuditEvents.java`** \u2014 the structured `OWNER_CREATED` event's field is renamed `customerCode` \u2192 `memberId` (JSON now emits `\"memberId\"`).\n\n- **`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 the human-readable audit line now logs `memberId` and drops `membershipNumber`.\n\n- **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 removed the `customerCode`, `checkDigit`, `membershipNumber` schema entries and added a `memberId` entry (regenerates `OwnerDto`).\n\n- **`resources/db/{h2,hsqldb,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`** \u2014 renamed the `customer_code` column to `member_id` and widened it to `VARCHAR(32)` (Postgres `TEXT`) to fit the longer id.\n\nRuntime confirmation from the audit log: `memberId=NSW2716E6609E1` (`NSW` + FY `27` + HASH8 `16E6609E` + CHK `1`), and the structured event `{\"seq\":1,\"ownerId\":11,\"memberId\":\"NSW2716E6609E1\",\"membershipLevel\":1,\"event\":\"OWNER_CREATED\"}`.",
